  "method": "Independent bootstrapped repositories and npm caches, same source and archive; large files contain independent incompressible data. Baseline follows installation in one checkout and cache warmup. Seeded mode directly charges primary seed; cold mode separately charges initialization and project cache priming, then installs in first workspace and charges layer save. The original warmed cache is preserved. Native installs both workspaces from its warmed cache offline. Source snapshot is cold in both modes. Both land into an unchecked integration branch; native fast-forwards the ref with an expected-old-value check. Dirty primary data remains in place. Readiness includes spawn and dependency preparation; first readiness excludes separately charged setup and seed, while firstReadyIncludingSeedSeconds includes both. Land-drop cumulative bytes show retained storage after retirement, cleanup cumulative bytes show retained storage after cache purge. Volume deltas are signed and include unrelated activity, metadata and delayed allocation. CPU/RSS unavailable portably; command wall time is measured. No savings threshold.",
